<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-3"><summary><span class="chapter-count">03</span><h3>Landscape Installation Services in Arvada Built for Colorado Conditions</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>Landscape installation in Colorado is technical work. Arvada sits at over 5,000 feet elevation — UV exposure is more intense, temperature swings are more extreme, and the soil is often clay-heavy with poor drainage. These aren’t problems a skilled landscape team can ignore. They’re variables that need to be designed around from the start.</p>
<p>Our installation teams have spent more than a decade working in these conditions. We prepare soil before planting, not just dig holes and fill them. We specify plants based on proven performance in Colorado’s climate zone — drought tolerance, frost hardiness, sun exposure — not just what’s available at the nursery that week. Irrigation systems are designed for Colorado’s evaporation rates and sized properly for each zone.</p>
<p>Hardscape elements — retaining walls, paver pathways, edging, and drainage features — are installed with Colorado’s ground movement in mind. Bases are dug and compacted correctly. Drainage is considered before it becomes a problem. The work is done once and done right, because remediation after a failed landscape installation costs far more than doing it properly the first time.<br/></p>
<p>We handle the full installation scope: grading and site prep, soil amendment, irrigation installation, planting, seeding or turf laying, hardscape, and cleanup. When we leave your property, the job is finished.</p>

<h3>Custom Landscape Designs for Every Arvada Property and Budget</h3>

<p>Arvada has a wide range of property styles — older established neighbourhoods close to Olde Town with mature trees and compact lots, mid-century homes in the central suburbs, and newer developments further west with larger yards and open layouts. Good landscape design adapts to the property it’s working with, not the other way around.</p>
<p>We design landscapes for all of it. Smaller Arvada lots get smart, edited designs that make the most of limited space — clean lines, low-maintenance plantings, and hardscape elements that extend usable square footage. Larger properties get designs that create structure and interest across the full yard, with defined zones for lawn, planting beds, outdoor living, and transition spaces that pull it all together.</p>
<p>Every design starts with a real site assessment and a conversation about how you use your property, what you want it to look like, and how much time you want to spend maintaining it. From there we develop a design that fits your yard, your lifestyle, and your budget — not a template with your address typed into it.<br/></p>
<p>We also handle phased projects for homeowners who want to build their landscape over time. We’ll design the full picture upfront and build it in stages that make sense financially and practically.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-4"><summary><span class="chapter-count">04</span><h3>Commercial Landscape Service in Arvada for Properties That Need to Perform</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>A well-maintained commercial landscape does real work for a business. It shapes first impressions, signals professionalism, and tells customers and tenants something about how a property is managed before they walk through the door. For commercial properties in Arvada, that first impression matters — and it starts at the kerb.</p>
<p>Ridgewell provides commercial landscape design and installation services for Arvada businesses, HOAs, and property managers. We work with commercial clients who need a landscape that looks intentional, holds up through Colorado’s seasons, and requires a realistic maintenance burden for the property team managing it.</p>
<p>Our commercial landscape work covers initial design and installation — not ongoing maintenance contracts. We design and build commercial landscapes that are practical from day one: appropriate plant selection for the site conditions, irrigation systems that don’t require constant adjustment, and hardscape and lawn elements that maintain their appearance with standard upkeep.<br/></p>
<p>We understand that commercial projects have schedules, stakeholders, and site constraints that residential projects don’t. Our process is built to accommodate that — clear scoping, straightforward communication, and installations that don’t disrupt your business operations more than necessary.</p>
</div>
</details>
