<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-8"><summary><span class="chapter-count">08</span><h3>What Arvada Homeowners and Business Owners Ask Us Most About Landscape Services</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><div class="content-feature">
<div id="eael-adv-accordion-c132f7d">
<div id="how-much-do-landscape-design-and-installation-services-cost-in-arvada-co-"><h3>How much do landscape design and installation services cost in Arvada, CO? </h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2021"><p>Landscape project costs in Arvada vary significantly based on scope, property size, and the mix of lawn, planting, hardscape, and irrigation work involved. A focused front yard redesign with new planting, edging, and sod typically starts around $5,000–$10,000. Full backyard landscape installations with hardscape elements, irrigation, and planting generally range from $15,000–$40,000. Larger or more complex projects — commercial properties, full property redesigns, or landscapes combined with significant hardscape — can exceed $50,000. We provide detailed, itemised quotes after an in-person site assessment so you know exactly what’s included before committing to anything.</p>
</div>

<div id="do-you-offer-commercial-landscape-services-in-arvada-"><h3>Do you offer commercial landscape services in Arvada? </h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2022"><p>Yes. We provide commercial landscape design and installation for businesses, HOAs, and property managers in Arvada. Our commercial work covers the design and build phase — creating a landscape that performs well, looks professional, and is manageable long-term for your property team. We work with commercial clients who have specific timelines, site constraints, and stakeholder requirements, and our process is structured to accommodate those needs.</p>
</div>

<div id="what-colorado-lawn-and-landscape-services-does-ridgewell-offer"><h3>What Colorado lawn and landscape services does Ridgewell offer?</h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2023"><p>We offer a full range of landscape design and installation services across Colorado, including: custom landscape design, lawn installation (sod and seed), planting bed design and installation, irrigation system installation, xeriscaping and water-wise landscaping, hardscape integration (patios, pathways, retaining walls), grading and drainage, and commercial landscape installation. We handle each project as a complete scope — design through installation — rather than offering individual services in isolation.</p>
</div>

<div id="do-i-need-a-landscape-designer-for-my-arvada-property-or-can-i-just-get-an-installation-quote"><h3>Do I need a landscape designer for my Arvada property, or can I just get an installation quote?</h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2024"><p>For most projects beyond basic lawn replacement, we recommend starting with a design. A proper design ensures the installation makes sense for your specific site — soil conditions, drainage, sun exposure, existing features, and how the different elements relate to each other. It also prevents costly changes mid-project. Our design and installation are integrated, so you get both from the same team without paying a separate designer and then finding a separate installer.</p>
</div>

<div id="how-long-does-landscape-installation-take-in-arvada-"><h3>How long does landscape installation take in Arvada? </h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2025"><p> Timeline depends heavily on project scope. A straightforward front yard refresh — sod, planting beds, edging — can be completed in a few days. A full backyard landscape installation with hardscape, irrigation, and planting typically takes 2–4 weeks. Larger or more complex projects take longer. We provide a realistic schedule before work begins and keep you updated throughout. We also work with clients on phased installations if the full project needs to be spread across time.</p>
</div>

<div id="can-you-do-xeriscaping-or-water-wise-landscaping-in-arvada-"><h3>Can you do xeriscaping or water-wise landscaping in Arvada? </h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2026"><p>Yes, and it’s something we actively recommend for Arvada homeowners given Colorado’s water restrictions and the increasing cost of irrigation. Xeriscaping doesn’t mean rocks and cacti — it means designing a landscape that’s beautiful and functional while using significantly less water. We design and install xeriscape landscapes that include drought-tolerant Colorado-native and adapted plants, efficient drip irrigation, and mulched planting beds that retain moisture and reduce maintenance. The result is a yard that looks great and costs less to maintain year-round.</p>
</div>

<div id="can-you-handle-both-the-landscaping-and-hardscape-for-my-arvada-backyard"><h3>Can you handle both the landscaping and hardscape for my Arvada backyard?</h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2027"><p>Yes — and combining both services with one contractor is the most efficient way to do a full backyard project. We design and install landscape and hardscape together, which means the planting and the patio, the lawn and the retaining wall, the irrigation and the drainage are all designed to work as a system. Projects where landscape and hardscape are handled by separate companies often end up with design inconsistencies and site conflicts that are expensive to resolve.</p>
</div>

